```java
import org.jsoup.Jsoup;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Document;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String html = "<html><body>Hello <b>World!</b></body></html>";
        
        // Parse the HTML using Jsoup
        Document doc = Jsoup.parse(html);
        
        // Print out the parsed HTML
        System.out.println("Parsed HTML:");
        System.out.println(doc.toString());
    }
}
```

When you run this program, it will print out the original HTML document that was passed into the `Jsoup.parse()` method.

To generate plain text from an HTML document, you can use a library like Jsoup. However, to create a new HTML document from scratch without any external libraries, you can use the following code:

```java
import org.jsoup.Jsoup;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Document;

public class DocumentGenerator {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String html = "<html><body>Hello <b>World!</b></body></html>";

        // Create a new HTML document from scratch
        Document doc = Jsoup.parse(html);

        // Print out the created HTML document as plain text
        System.out.println("Created HTML as Plain Text:");
        System.out.println(doc.toString());
    }
}
```

When you run this program, it will print out the original HTML document that was passed into the `Jsoup.parse()` method.
